  "handbook_failure_semantics": "Each commit attempt clears publication_possible. A failed attempt returns typed CommitFailure with Publication::NotPublished or Publication::Indeterminate. The CLI reads this typed result; prior attempts cannot contaminate this attempt classification. Earlier successful publication remains real and cannot be canceled.",
  "handbook_replay_guard_semantics": "CLI read_only modifier applies only to generic tx. Terminal request replay retains coordinated publication repair through a writable transaction. The API rejects read-only commit with replay=true as typed NotPublished; normal read-only commit closes with Unchanged."
